# `assets/` is a byte-faithful mirror of what the pipeline produced, so nothing
# under it may be line-ending converted.
#
# This repository is developed on Windows with `core.autocrlf=true`, and most of
# the text in `assets/extracted/` -- `.shader`, `.skin`, `.cfg`, the readmes --
# is id Software and OpenArena material authored on Windows and genuinely CRLF.
# Without this rule `git add` rewrites it to LF on the way in and checkout
# rewrites it back on the way out, and neither round trip is the identity:
# `default.cfg` lost 108 bytes that way. A tree committed so it can be restored
# has to restore to the bytes `extract-pk3.mjs` wrote, or the shader parser and
# every hash over it are reading something upstream never shipped.
assets/** -text
